# Public User Modes (7)

These are the **user-facing modes** shown in the UI. Users choose one depending on their needs; internally, each mode may use one or more internal techniques.

## Mode A — Fast (Proxy)
**Goal:** Fastest and cheapest browsing through the service.

**What the user gets**
- Normal page loading through the service
- Best-effort compatibility

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 2 (server-side fetch & rewrite)
- May lightly apply Internal Mode 6 (basic optimization)

**Best for**
- Simple websites, static content, basic pages

**Known limitations**
- Some modern sites may break (CSP, heavy JS apps, bot protections)

---

## Mode B — Fast+ (Proxy Optimized)
**Goal:** Same as Fast, but optimized for slower devices/networks and improved success rate.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 2 (proxy rewrite)
- Internal Mode 6 (transcoding/optimization)
- May leverage Internal Mode 9 (existing proxy engine) for reliability

**Best for**
- Heavier pages where speed/bandwidth matters

**Known limitations**
- Aggressive optimization may occasionally break page layout/functionality

---

## Mode C — Reader (Article View)
**Goal:** Extract and show the main readable content.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 4 (reader/content extraction)

**Best for**
- News, blogs, documentation, guides

**Known limitations**
- Not suitable for web apps or complex interactions

---

## Mode D — Text-only (Ultra)
**Goal:** Maximum compatibility and minimal bandwidth.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 5 (text-only)

**Best for**
- Very slow connections
- When other modes fail
- Accessibility / minimal UI needs

**Known limitations**
- Minimal visuals and reduced interactivity

---

## Mode E — Snapshot (View-only)
**Goal:** Load using a real browser once, then replay a captured version.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 8 (snapshot/replay)
- Often created using Internal Mode 3 (Playwright/Puppeteer) to generate the snapshot

**Best for**
- View-only pages, quick sharing, low-cost access to JS-heavy pages without live sessions

**Known limitations**
- Not fully interactive
- Dynamic updates and some login flows may not work well

---

## Mode F — Live (Interactive)
**Goal:** Interactive browsing where the real page runs on the server.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 3 (rendering-as-image / CDP streaming via Playwright/Puppeteer)
- May use Internal Mode 7 (selective remote rendering) to reduce cost

**Best for**
- Modern JS apps
- Sites that break in proxy mode

**Known limitations**
- Higher server cost
- Latency depending on network and server load
- Audio/video may be limited depending on implementation

---

## Mode G — Full Desktop (Maximum)
**Goal:** Maximum compatibility via a full remote desktop browser.

**Internally uses**
- Internal Mode 1 (Guacamole/noVNC)

**Best for**
- Long sessions
- Downloads and complex workflows
- Maximum compatibility requirements

**Known limitations**
- Highest server cost
- Requires strict isolation and abuse prevention

